{"title":"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ravindra and Hongshu made a pizza together. Ravindra ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the pizza. Hongshu ate half as much as Ravindra. What percentage of the original pizza was left?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/99794ca06fdf619468cb068a4d8f126e35bbbff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 30 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 50 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the numbers given in the problem, we can see that Hongshu ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e991e6adedb7eb689b7e00f8175d3d4b66aac731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} \\div 2 = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> of the pizza.\n</p><p>Summing the fractions to see how much pizza they ate, we can see that they ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6faf3a38cfdf69c2d315e104bca084327a8f89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{2 + 1}{5} = \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" /> of the pizza.\n</p><p>We now need to subtract this from the whole pizza to see how much pizza is remaining. We can then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7b3e4b0726ed0ec6f21d1598f249b01afe4e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{5} - \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> of the pizza is remaining.\n</p><p>Converting this to a percentage, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1488dbcd4259301f23d119806a1727fd84be46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2}{5} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{200}{5}\\% = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 40}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"291\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Converting the amount of pizza that Ravindra ate into a percentage, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d406e93da25291dc965c6b3635df73ac27894b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2}{5} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{200}{5}\\% = 40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"245\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since Hongshu ate half of that, he ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3927acd9c858d460703c6ccc68c0942fb7890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\% \\div 2 = 20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" /> of the pizza.\n</p><p>Summing the percentages to see how much pizza they ate in total, we can see that they ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b9c71df5435321e24ca1a95ef783aaa08ae004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\% + 20\\% = 60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"17\" /> of the pizza in total.\n</p><p>Subtracting this from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> of the pizza, which is the whole pizza, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a012f49b707cc224ffc5aa544bc24a92be6dedab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 60\\% = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 40}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"204\" height=\"30\" /> of the pizza remains.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal\">2006 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" s